Usage: xnvme perf run [<uri>...] [<args>]

Run a time-bounded async IO benchmark against one or more NVMe devices.
Devices are distributed across CPU threads pinned by --cpumask or --cpulist.

Positional arguments:

  [uri ...]                     ; Device URI e.g. '/dev/nvme0n1', '0000:01:00.1', '10.9.8.1:8888', '\\.\PhysicalDrive1'

Where <args> include:

  --iopattern STRING            ; IO pattern (read, write, randread, randwrite)
  [ --nqueues NUM ]             ; Number of queues per device
  --qdepth NUM                  ; Use given 'NUM' as queue max capacity
  --iosize NUM                  ; Use given 'NUM' as bs/iosize
  --runtime NUM                 ; Run for 'NUM' seconds
  [ --cpumask STRING ]          ; Hex CPU bitmask for thread pinning (e.g. 0x3)
  [ --cpulist STRING ]          ; Comma-separated list of CPU ids or CPU id ranges for thread pinning (e.g. 0-3,4,6)

With <args> for backend:

  [ --be STRING ]               ; xNVMe backend, e.g. 'spdk', 'libvfn', 'upcie'
  [ --subnqn STRING ]           ; Subsystem NQN of the NVMe over Fabrics endpoint e.g. 'nqn.2022-06.io.xnvme:ctrlnode1'
  [ --direct ]                  ; Bypass layers
  [ --poll_io NUM ]             ; For async={io_uring,libaio,kqueue}, enable hipri/io-compl.polling
  [ --poll_sq NUM ]             ; For async=io_uring, enable kernel-side sqthread-poll
  [ --gpu_id NUM ]              ; For be=upcie-cuda/upcie-hip, GPU ordinal to use
  [ --homi-id NUM ]             ; The HOMI identifier to share controllers under
  [ --report-freq FLOAT ]       ; Report progress every 'FLOAT' seconds
  [ --help ]                    ; Show usage / help

See 'xnvme perf --help' for other commands

xnvme perf - IO benchmarks against xNVMe devices -- ver: {major: 0, minor: 7, patch: 5, vcs: 'be83e57'}
